Z||000011||artherd||10-15-2001||05:09 AM||||Hey Tina, WOW!!!<P>It'd be an honor to get beaten by your car, I hope all those confident males you spanked appricated it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Welcome to the 12-second club  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>(and you thought just silver cars are addicitive?  Welcome to the wonderful world of CAR RACING!!)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000012||KissMySSFiero||10-15-2001||07:45 AM||||congrats.<BR>what tranny are you running now?  and how is your clutch holding up?  Dont you have archies inthere?  does it hold up better than the other clutches you had?   <BR>I cant wait til winter.   time to start tearing into my car....hmmmmm coulda had a V8.<BR><P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Tina||10-15-2001||01:01 PM||||Thanks guys.<BR>Like I said earlier, WHAT A BLAST.And aside from a few select "Mustang products", everybody was super nice and really helpful. Engine-rumble wise though, ...Holy Cow...<BR>my ears finally stopped ringing late last evening.<BR>O.K., on to Business                  <P>The Izuzu 5 speed and Archie's centerforce<BR>held up well.<BR>The clutch grabbed hard everytime.<BR>(No slippage whatsoever)Kudos, to Archie  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Now my tires where a different story,lot's a spin there. <BR>(gotta go shopping, baby needs a new pair of shoes )  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Jimmy,guess we missed each other again.<BR>But here you go.<BR>1st run .... too pathetic to post...<BR>2nd <BR>    R/T ... 1.090<BR>    60' ... 1.870<BR>    330 ... 5.399<BR>    1/8 ... 8.331<BR>    MPH ... 83.88<BR>    1000... 10.812<BR>    1/4 ... 12.931<BR>    MPH ... 106.95<P>3rd and final<BR>  Dial ... 12.90<BR>    RT ... 1.261<BR>    60'... 2.503<BR>    330... 6.408<BR>    1/8... 9.503<BR>    MPH... 80.07<BR>   1000... 12.059<BR>    1/4... 14.096<BR>    MPH... 105.78<P>Guess, a lot of practice is in order <BR>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>   <P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula88||10-15-2001||02:45 PM||||Thanks, Tina, for re-affirming my belief that there are some cool gearhead chicks out there who are into their cars and <B><I>DRIVE</B></I> them!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>12 Second Fiero V8!  OH YEAH!! <P>Hope to run into you at a drag strip some day - or a show.  Racing's more fun though!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><FONT SIZE="1">Note: The terms "gearhead" and "chick" are used as compliments and are not meant to stereotype or degrade anyone in any way.  Your mileage may vary. Signed: A gearhead dude.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
