Z||000019||California Kid||10-15-2001||04:43 PM||||Tina,<BR>Next time you go to the track, if you're getting the same amount of tire spin, try dropping the hammer on the first yellow. I got my best runs by doing this, didn't red light, and caused some of the competition to red light in the process. Takes a little experimentation with launch rpm, but it will hook up pretty good right at the stage lights.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Tina||10-15-2001||04:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B><FONT SIZE="1">Note: The terms "gearhead" and "chick" are used as compliments and are not meant to stereotype or degrade anyone in any way.  Your mileage may vary. Signed: A gearhead dude.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></FONT><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ROFL<P>Tina<BR>BTW Just got back from the "Tire-Guy".<BR>    Doesn't look too good.<BR>    There really doesn't seem to be a whole <BR>    lot out there for us Fiero drivers.<BR>     <P>||||reg||1
Z||000021||MinnGreenGT||10-15-2001||05:04 PM||||Tina- Just thinking about your tire dilemma and recalled reading this from 1FST2M6<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><BR>I'd shy away from the BFGs just cause they are so pricey and the Yoko or Falken are just as sticky and will out last the BFGs. <BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It came from this thread if you're interested in the source of the discussion... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014347.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/014347.html</A> <P>Don't know if this helps or not...good luck.  <P>BTW: Awsome run!  Maybe next year we need to make a "meeting/event" out of heading over to the track!  I'm sure we'd get quite a few takers if we plan it far enough in advance.  That would certainly make a Fiero-impression on the spectators.<P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 10-15-2001).]||||reg||1
